    "insert": "\nEnsure the provisional title aligns with the theme and purpose of the exposé, while being creative and specific. The title should be thematically consistent with the goal of the learning environment to be developed.\nThe title accurately describes the proposal's intent to develop a goal-oriented learning environment using LLMs. The acronym is a creative way to capture the reader's interest and combines the technical details directly with its practical application.\nThe title can be left in its current form.\n\nPresent a compelling and focused introduction to captivate the audience. The hook should highlight why there is such an urgent need for a goal-oriented learning environment.\nThe hook contains surprising facts and is a good starting point for research as it addresses a problem that older people want to learn something new but cannot for various reasons.\n\nProvide a detailed description of the problems that arises from learning new things.\nThe problems has been identified as prospective students doesn't exactly know what you have to need to learn before you wan't to learn a specific thing.\n\nDefine the stakeholders involved in the learning environment.\nThe stakeholders are clearly identified for people starting at age 25.\n\nOutline the existing approach for solving the need of a learning environment and identify their limitations. Clearly articulate the gaps of the current approach, you want to solve.\nGaps of current approaches has been outlined by missing personalized learning paths and a solution with LLMs has been proposed.\n\nEnsure the research questions are clear, focused and actionable. \nThe questions are useful for finding out the optimal conditions for the learning environment. Sub-RQ 2.1 should perhaps be reformulated as in the annotation or phrased in such a way that it is checked beforehand whether positive learning experiences and learning progress need to be weighed against each other at all.\n\n"
